  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T246 - ACT4 - Dragonstone Blood Price at first light"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-essos/frame-246.jpg"

  "Before sunrise, Daenerys's envoys arrive with lacquered chests and a contract that reads like a command. Daario points to the harbor mouth where your transport cogs wait under crosswind and says plainly that half your allied banners will drift away unless you prove immediate solvency. A faction inside your own coalition demands visible guarantees by dawn or they will negotiate separately with your enemies.

The blood price here is not metaphor. If this deal fails, underpaid mercenaries will strip nearby villages for provisions, and every corpse will be counted against your name. A public oath gives you legitimacy and may steady frightened allies. A private coercion campaign can secure signatures faster, but once fear is your currency, every renewal gets pricier.

The eastern sky pales over masts and siege timber. You can still decide whether Valehart rules by lawful confidence or by managed terror, but not whether someone pays this morning."

