__section

section__
  @title "T248 - ACT4 - The Dreadfort Border Muster in crowded galleries"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "close"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-essos/frame-248.jpg"

  "At the slave quay, your captains assemble in a half-circle of salt-stiff cloaks while Illyrio's agents carry locked coffers through customs. The muster reports from the Dreadfort frontier are grim: riders need pay and fodder now, and rumor says two companies are already shopping their swords to your enemies. Jorah keeps the meeting orderly, but even he cannot hide that discipline is running on fumes.

This choice is about coherence. If you keep faith with northern remittances despite Pentoshi pressure, allies may hold their line and your command stays legible. If you answer shortfall with clandestine threats against brokers and families, money arrives faster and fear restores obedience for a while. Then fear starts billing interest.

The quay stones are slick beneath your boots, and somewhere beyond the warehouses a horse screams as if it has already seen tomorrow's battlefield."

  choice__
