section__
  @title "T249 - ACT4 - The Eyrie Crown Ultimatum by candle smoke"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-essos/frame-249.jpg"

  "Candle smoke pools under the orange trees in Illyrio's upper court while a Vale envoy reads an ultimatum from the Eyrie. The wording is courteous and absolute: release two hostages and certify your foreign loans by dawn, or the mountain roads close to every Valehart cart. Jorah keeps one hand on his sword pommel. The ship factors keep their eyes on your signet ring.

This is the price of overlapping wars. If you satisfy the Vale publicly, eastern creditors may treat you as weak and raise rates before next tide. If you satisfy the creditors first, western allies will call you captive to Essosi coin and peel away from your coalition. The choice is not between good and bad policy. It is between which political front you can afford to inflame tonight.

Wax spits in the brazier, and the parchment already smells singed. The first seal you break will tell the realm whether Valehart governs by visible law or by private leverage."

  choice__
    @target "T250 - ACT4 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "File the Eyrie terms before harbor magistrates, accept the delay and scrutiny, and preserve public legitimacy across allied courts"
  __choice

