section__
  @title "T250 - ACT4 - Pentos Harbor Ambush in river fog"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-essos/frame-250.jpg"

  "Fog rolls in from Blackwater traffic and turns Pentos harbor into a maze of mast shadows. A courier from Daenerys reports that one of your grain cogs was boarded before dawn by men in neutral cloaks, then released with half the cargo gone and all manifests burned. Daario wants immediate retaliation. The merchant princes want proof, indemnity, and higher insurance before they load another sack.

Raven copies of the incident are already spreading with three contradictory versions, each one damaging to you in a different way. If you answer publicly, you might steady confidence and keep contracts enforceable, but you reveal your routes. If you strike in secret, shipments may move faster, yet every partner will assume you can be manipulated by panic. A third path is to outsource force entirely and pay strangers to impose order.

Wet hemp slaps the pier posts while stevedores wait for your word. Whoever controls the next convoy controls your campaign tempo."

  choice__
    @target "T251 - ACT4 - Qarth Alliance Split near the godswood"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
