  __choice
__section

section__
  @title "T252 - ACT4 - The Wall War Map against old law"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "wide"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-essos/frame-252.jpg"

  "A black-cloaked courier from the Wall unrolls a grease-stained campaign map across Illyrio's counting table. Wildling movement has shifted east, supply depots are thin, and the Watch asks for iron, lamp oil, and pay advances that your Essosi bankers call nonrecoverable charity. While the courier speaks, sellsword captains in your service ask why their arrears should wait for men they will never meet.

Strategically, this is the old law against new finance. Funding the frontier openly can stabilize your northern flank and prove you still honor commitments beyond immediate profit. Diverting those funds through covert accounts keeps your southern operations liquid, but once discovered it will brand you as a lord who leverages existential threats as bargaining chips.

The map corners curl in the heat, and the inked line of the Wall looks thinner than memory. Whatever you choose, someone important will decide you have declared your true priorities."

  choice__
    @target "T253 - ACT4 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
    @action honor = clampStat(honor + 1, 0, 30)
    @action essos_ties = clampStat(essos_ties + 1, 0, 30)
    @action war_readiness = clampStat(war_readiness + 1, 0, 30)
    @action survival_clock = clampStat(survival_clock - 1, 0, 30)
    "Commit Watch support through declared ledgers and sworn witnesses, accepting near-term budget pain to uphold lawful obligations"
  __choice

  choice__
    @target "T254 - ACT4 - Moat Cailin Whispered Warning at the gatehouse"
