section__
  @title "T253 - ACT4 - Castle Black Inheritance Claim under moonless sky"
  @textPacing "cinematic"
  @shot "medium"
  @backdrop "https://example.com/thrones/04-act4-essos/frame-253.jpg"

  "In a shuttered warehouse above the quay, a notarized claim arrives naming a new commander at Castle Black and challenging debts signed by the old one. Illyrio's brokers immediately demand renegotiation of every northern shipment tied to Watch guarantees. Jorah warns that if this legal fight drags, frontier garrisons will miss rations before the next moon and blame Valehart for the gap.

Politically, the inheritance dispute is a trap. Backing the claim in open process might protect your honor with northern houses, but it could freeze coin when speed matters most. Forcing a result through covert pressure keeps caravans moving, yet the moment northern scribes uncover tampering, your credibility in every future oath hearing collapses.

Outside, chain hoists screech as cargo swings over black water. You need one signature path that keeps supplies moving without teaching allies that your promises expire under financial strain."

