Your captains already read uncertainty as weakness. A transparent decree could rebuild command coherence and reassure allies who still treat Valehart as a lawful broker. A covert purge could stop collapse overnight, but it also creates a chain of men who obey only under threat and sell secrets to survive. In Act 4, discipline purchased with fear does not stay cheap.

Rain drums on tile above the counting chamber while clerks sand wet ink. The order you issue here decides whether your army follows instructions or just follows terror."

