  "A cipher from Oldtown reaches Pentos hidden inside a maester's shipping invoice. The message names two Valehart intermediaries who have been selling your fleet timings to rival houses for months, then billing both sides for secrecy. Daenerys calls it predictable treachery in wartime. The merchant princes call it a market adjustment and ask what premium you will pay for cleaner channels.

You can expose the traitors in open court, seize accounts, and prove that Valehart punishes fraud by law. That move strengthens long-term confidence but costs precious days while evidence is argued. Or you can run a quiet counterintelligence cutout, feeding false schedules until your enemies ambush empty water. Faster, bloodier, and guaranteed to multiply private enemies.

Hot pitch fumes drift from the shipwright yard while your scribes await dictation. This decision determines whether your network is rebuilt on institutions or on fear of your next unseen hand."

