You are not just swapping prisoners. You are pricing maritime coercion for the next act. A public, witnessed exchange could calm allied nerves and lock partner houses into accountable behavior. A hidden bargain can extract better terms tonight, but it teaches every captain that Valehart agreements are negotiable at knife point.

Tar smoke from repair braziers mixes with salt and rot while the tide climbs the stones. By dawn, either your sea policy has rules or it has predators."

