Your ration masters are already cutting issue by loyalty, and every officer knows it. If you endorse the Highgarden bargain in open assembly, you may steady a brittle coalition with clear obligations. If you lock terms in private, you can squeeze better concessions now, but every unpaid captain will assume you made another hidden hierarchy of winners and losers.

Spiced wine goes warm in silver cups while your scribes wait for whichever seal you choose to break. This is less a contract than a declaration of how Valehart intends to survive the winter war."

