The prisoner's information could reopen your overland route and expose who has been buying your convoy schedules. It could also be bait planted to make Valehart strike the wrong rivals in public. If you process his confession on record, you gain legitimacy and risk losing tempo. If you break him in private, you might move faster, but your enemies will call every later accusation fabricated.

The room smells of rust, lamp oil, and old rope. This is a choice between trusted procedure and speed purchased with fear."

